# Chroma library, modern Earth: THE SPHERES OF SOCIETY, Protection life moments. Library thread, 2026-10-09, "v22"
# update stage 4, item 15 phase 3 (chroma-ideas/spheres-implementation.md sections 2, 4 "Library" and 5): the moments
# named in spheres-data/prot.json character.moments, as ordinary moments with their own rates. Every moment carries
# sphere: prot, every option the face it acts in (prot.R; a cross option X>Y the means colour's face; a pair option the
# wheel-order pair face, WR as .RW, WG as .GW, UG as .GU). Syntax: header of build.py. Rules: SPEC.md.
#
# Skipped as already written: 'the call-up letter, or the horn' is 'the call to serve' (earth-world-civic.lib); 'the
# day the war ends' is 'the ceasefire holds' (ready/earth-spheres-ev-prot.lib) and 'long tables in the street when the
# war ends' (ready/earth-spheres-ev-gather.lib); the 'first time they are arrested' half of its moment is 'the police at
# the door' and 'the first night in a cell', so only the first arrest one makes is written here.
#
# Everyday pairs (one calls two colours, its partner the other three, same stages and ages): the stranger on the dark
# road BRG (s1) with the young one who learns to stand their ground WU (s3); the first night on watch WRG (s2) with the
# envelope at the car window UB (s4), both at the watch.
# Life events and their pair sets: the first day in uniform D1a, visiting a brother or sister inside D1b, the memorial
# D2a, the neighbour's door D2b, the first arrest D3a, the break-in D3b, the comrade lost D4a, the crash on the road
# D4b, the farewell at the gate D5a, coming home changed D6a, the first fire call D6b.
# Evenness: in every moment each one-colour option has one chance, each cross option one chance, each pair option one
# chance (everyday 75 and 65, life events 65 and 55), so each colour's mean is the same in every stage. No flags.
# Safety: violence stays off-page; no option uses force on anyone beyond a lawful arrest told plainly; no child is
# harmed; nobody under 18 serves in a watch, a crew or the forces (those moments open at 18 or later); nothing sexual.

# ================================================================ the dark road and the young one (all adults)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls BRG (cycle s1); partner: a young one learns to stand their ground

== a stranger waving a torch on the dark road
tier: everyday
sphere: prot
stages: young_adult+
age: 18-95
calls: BRG
rate: .5
share: .25
tone: mixed
life: safety, strangers
horizon: moment
roles: friend
earth: driving home late on the empty road, you see a stranger by a broken-down car, waving a torch at you
times: Coming on a stranger in need on a lonely road at night, and choosing whether to stop, comes to about 1 in 4 lives, once or a few times (estimate)
likelier: country roads, night driving for work, a remote home, a long commute
rarer: city life without a car, no travel at night
gap: 3-15
scene: Late at night on the empty road out of {place}, {Ns} headlights find a car on the verge with its bonnet up. A stranger in a thin coat steps out, waving a torch. The nearest house is miles back.
scene W: Anyone stuck out here deserves help, and the road has its rules for this too: hazard lights, a safe distance, a call to the right people.
scene U: {N} slows and looks hard: one person or more, a real breakdown or not, and where the next lit place is.
scene B: {N} has heard the stories about stops like this one. {Ns} own safety comes first, and then everyone else's.
scene R: Whoever it is, they are cold and alone out here. {Ns} foot is already on the brake.
scene G: Out here people stop for each other; it is how it has always been. But {N} has never seen this face before.
- W | stop at a safe distance with hazards on, and call the breakdown line for them | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: prot.W | chance: 75
- U | pull up ahead with the engine running, and talk through the window first | v: security, self-direction | sphere: prot.U | chance: 75
- B | drive on, and ring the police from the next lit petrol station | v: security | sphere: prot.B | chance: 75
- R | pull over, jump out, and help with the car in the dark | v: benevolence, stimulation | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: prot.R | chance: 75
- G | ask who their people are in the valley, then drive them to the village | v: benevolence, tradition | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: prot.G | chance: 75
- W>U | stop, take the car's details, and send them to the roadside service in a message | v: conformity, security | tech: phone | sphere: prot.W | chance: 65
- U>B | ring a friend with the stranger's number plate before you unlock a door | act: ring a friend with the stranger's number plate before they unlock a door | v: security | sphere: prot.U | chance: 65
- B>R | offer a lift to town for the price of the petrol, and enjoy the company | v: hedonism, achievement | sphere: prot.B | chance: 65
- R>G | flag down the next car too, so the two drivers can tow them home | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: prot.R | chance: 65
- G>W | wait with them in your warm car until the recovery truck comes | act: wait with them in their warm car until the recovery truck comes | v: benevolence | sphere: prot.G | chance: 65
works: The stranger turns out to be a nurse coming off a late shift, and the night ends with a hot drink and thanks.
works: Help comes, the car starts, and {N} drives home feeling the night has been put right.
fails: {N} spends an hour in the cold for nothing: the stranger gets a lift with someone else and does not even wave.
fails: {N} drives home uneasy, and all week cannot decide whether they chose well.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WU (cycle s3); partner: a stranger waving a torch on the dark road

== a young one learns to stand their ground
tier: everyday
sphere: prot
stages: young_adult+
age: 18-95
calls: WU
rate: .5
share: .25
tone: mixed
life: family, school
horizon: months
roles: sibling, parent
who: sibling
earth: your brother's or sister's youngest is being picked on at school, and asks you how to make it stop
times: Bullying touches a large minority of schoolchildren at some point (school surveys vary widely); being the older relative a young one turns to about it comes to about 1 in 4 lives, once or twice (estimate)
likelier: brothers and sisters with young children, a large family nearby, a person the young ones look up to
rarer: no young relatives, a family scattered far apart
gap: 3-12
scene: {sibling}'s youngest, ten years old, has gone quiet. At last it comes out: two older children take his lunch and call him names at the school gate, and he asks {N}, of all people, how to make it stop.
scene W: Schools have rules for this, and grown-ups whose job it is to keep them. {N} wants him to know he has every right to be safe.
scene U: {N} wants to know exactly what happens, where and when, before giving a word of advice.
scene B: {N} remembers being ten: the ones who were left alone were the ones who seemed not to care.
scene R: It makes {N} furious. {N} would march down to that gate tomorrow if he let them.
scene G: In this family nobody stands alone. He should know that his cousins, aunts and uncles are behind him.
- W | help him tell his teacher, and go with him to say it | v: security, conformity | sphere: prot.W | chance: 75
- U | ask him for every detail, and work out with him when it happens | v: self-direction, security | sphere: prot.U | chance: 75
- B | teach him to shrug, look bored, and never let them see it lands | v: self-direction, power | sphere: prot.B | chance: 75
- R | practise it with him, loud and clear: look them in the eye and say no | v: stimulation, self-direction | sphere: prot.R | chance: 75
- G | ask his cousins at the same school to walk with him at break | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: prot.G | chance: 75
- W>R | stand at the gate with him the first morning, in plain sight, saying nothing | v: benevolence, security | sphere: prot.W | chance: 65
- U>G | find out which friends he has, and help him spend break with them | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: prot.U | chance: 65
- B>W | write the head a cool, firm letter with every date, and expect a reply | v: power, security | sphere: prot.B | chance: 65
- R>U | take him to the judo club on Saturdays, for the balance and the nerve | v: stimulation, achievement | sphere: prot.R | chance: 65
- G>B | have a word with the school caretaker, an old family friend, to keep an eye out | v: tradition, security | sphere: prot.G | chance: 65
works: Within a term the name-calling stops, and he walks to school with his head up.
works: He comes to {N} once more, months later, only to say that it worked.
fails: It gets worse before it gets better, and his parents wish {N} had stayed out of it.
fails: He shrugs and stops talking about it, and {N} cannot tell whether it has stopped or only gone quiet.

# ================================================================ the watch (prot.watch)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WRG (cycle s2); partner: an envelope held out at the car window

== the first night on watch
tier: everyday
sphere: prot
haunt: prot.watch
ladder: newcomer
stages: young_adult+
age: 18-80
calls: WRG
rate: 2
share: .9
once: yes
tone: mixed
life: work, safety
horizon: moment
roles: mentor
who: mentor
earth: your first night shift on watch: the town asleep, an older hand beside you, and a radio that might go at any minute
times: Among newcomers to the watch (haunt prot.watch: the police, a guard post or the street's own rota), the first night on watch comes within weeks and to nearly all of them, once (estimate); outside the watch it never comes
likelier: a new recruit, a volunteer on a neighbours' rota, a night guard's first week
rarer: day work only, a desk post from the start
gap: 1-2
scene: {N}'s first night on watch. {mentor} has walked these streets for twenty years and says little; the town is asleep, the radio crackles now and then, and at two in the morning they find a shop door on the parade standing open.
scene W: {N} has learned the rules by heart: what to write, whom to call, how far to go and no further. Tonight they find out what the rules feel like in the dark.
scene U: {N} notices everything: which windows are lit, which cars are new on the street, the times on the shop clocks.
scene B: The night shift is where names are made. {N} wants {mentor} to tell the others the new one is good.
scene R: {Ns} heart has been going since the briefing. Half of {N} hopes the radio stays quiet; the other half hopes it does not.
scene G: These are the streets {N} grew up on. Behind every door is someone {N} might know by name.
- W | check the open door by the book, and log every step of it | v: conformity, security | sphere: prot.W | chance: 75
- U | stop and look before going in: the lock, the glass, the floor | v: self-direction, security | sphere: prot.U | chance: 75
- B | let the old hand go first, and watch how it is done | v: security, achievement | sphere: prot.B | chance: 75
- R | go in first with the torch, before the old hand can stop you | act: go in first with the torch, before the old hand can stop them | v: stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: prot.R | chance: 75
- G | ring the shopkeeper, whose number you know, before anything else | act: ring the shopkeeper, whose number they know, before anything else | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: prot.G | chance: 75
- W>B | write the night up so well the sergeant reads it out at shift change | v: achievement, conformity | sphere: prot.W | chance: 65
- U>R | follow the fresh footprints down the alley at a run | v: stimulation, self-direction | sphere: prot.U | chance: 65
- B>G | buy the old hand a tea at the all-night stall, and ask about the beat | v: tradition, achievement | mark: made a friend | sphere: prot.B | chance: 65
- R>W | move on the group shouting by the cash machine, then log it properly | v: security, stimulation | sphere: prot.R | chance: 65
- G>U | ask the night baker which cars do not belong on the street | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: prot.G | chance: 65
works: The open door turns out to be a forgotten lock, and {mentor} says {N} handled it as well as anyone could.
works: By dawn {N} knows the beat by night, and the shift becomes a story told well at breakfast.
fails: {N} misses something {mentor} sees at once, and hears about it at shift change.
fails: The night is long and cold, and {N} goes home wondering whether this work is for them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls UB (cycle s4); partner: the first night on watch

== an envelope held out at the car window
tier: everyday
sphere: prot
haunt: prot.watch
ladder: regular
stages: young_adult+
age: 18-80
calls: UB
rate: .5
share: .3
tone: trouble
life: work, honesty
horizon: week
roles: colleague, boss
who: colleague
earth: on a late stop, the driver holds out folded notes, and your partner on the shift says he is a friend of the inspector's
times: Among regulars of the watch (police, guards, inspectors at a gate), being offered a bribe or asked by a colleague to leave something out of a report comes to about 3 in 10 over a working life, once or a few times (estimate; surveys of police corruption vary widely by place)
likelier: a place where small bribes are usual, low pay, a senior who looks away, night work, a busy road or port
rarer: a force with strict oversight, good pay, a quiet village beat
gap: 3-10
scene: Past midnight {N} stops a van with no lights. The driver, a known local businessman, holds out folded notes and says nobody needs to write anything down. {colleague} murmurs that he is a friend of the inspector's, and to let it go.
scene W: The law says what happens at a stop, and it says the same for the inspector's friends as for anyone. {N} knows it.
scene U: {N} wonders what is in the back of the van that is worth this much to keep out of a report.
scene B: The notes come to more than a week's pay. And the inspector's friends have long memories, either way.
scene R: The man's easy smile makes {N} angry. He thinks everyone has a price.
scene G: {N} has to work beside {colleague} every night for years. What they do here, they do as a pair.
- W | hand back the notes, and write the stop up exactly as it happened | v: conformity, universalism | sphere: prot.W | chance: 75
- U | ask to see in the back of the van before you decide anything | act: ask to see in the back of the van before they decide anything | v: self-direction | sphere: prot.U | chance: 75
- B | take the notes, let him go, and keep the inspector's friend sweet | v: power, security | mark: hid a wrong | lever: subvert | sphere: prot.B | chance: 75
- R | tell him to put his money away before you add a charge for it | act: tell him to put his money away before they add a charge for it | v: stimulation, universalism | sphere: prot.R | chance: 75
- G | wave him on without the money, and stand by your partner on the shift | act: wave him on without the money, and stand by their partner on the shift | v: tradition, security | lever: neglect | sphere: prot.G | chance: 75
- W>G | refuse the notes, and talk your partner round to writing it up with you | act: refuse the notes, and talk their partner round to writing it up with them | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: prot.W | chance: 65
- U>W | note the plate and the time, and take it to the complaints office | v: universalism, security | lever: voice | pushes: institution police | sphere: prot.U | chance: 65
- B>U | let him go, and keep the favour he owes you on file | act: let him go, and keep the favour he owes them on file | v: power | lever: subvert | sphere: prot.B | chance: 65
- R>B | let him think you will take it, then charge him with the offer too | act: let him think they will take it, then charge him with the offer too | v: stimulation, power | sphere: prot.R | chance: 65
- G>R | tell your partner straight, out by the car, that you two do not do this | act: tell their partner straight, out by the car, that the two of them do not do this | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: voice | pushes: close colleague | sphere: prot.G | chance: 65
works: The stop is written up as it happened, and months later {N} is glad of every line of it.
works: {N} comes through it with a clear name, and {colleague} with a little more respect than before.
fails: The inspector hears of the night, and {N} finds the next rota full of the worst shifts.
fails: Whatever {N} chose follows them for a long time: a look in the canteen, a word behind their back.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: the first arrest one makes (pairs D3a)

== the first arrest you make
tier: life event
sphere: prot
haunt: prot.watch
ladder: newcomer
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-65
per_year: 0 0 .4 .3 .2 0
drivers: trouble+.3 unrest+.2
once: yes
times: Among newcomers to the watch (haunt prot.watch), the first arrest comes within a year or two to most police recruits and more rarely to guards and rota volunteers, once (estimate); outside the watch it never comes
likelier: a busy town beat, night shifts, a recruit on the streets rather than at a desk
rarer: a quiet village beat, a guard post with no power of arrest, a desk post
gap: 1-3
tone: mixed
life: work, justice
horizon: months
roles: mentor
who: mentor
earth: your first arrest: a man at the back of the builders' yard with a bag of copper pipe, as frightened as you are
scene: Past midnight {N} finds a man in his forties at the back of the builders' yard with a bag of copper pipe. He does not run. He says he has three children and no work, and {mentor} is still a street away.
scene W: The law does not change for a sad story, and it does not let {N} be rough with him either. Both halves matter tonight.
scene U: Copper pipe goes somewhere. {N} wonders who buys it, and how many yards have been stripped this month.
scene B: A clean first arrest gets noticed at the station. {N} knows the sergeant reads every one.
scene R: {Ns} pulse is racing. He is bigger than {N}, and the gate is behind him.
scene G: {N} thinks the face is familiar: one of the families from the estate by the canal, perhaps.
- W | caution him, arrest him by the book, and treat him with courtesy | v: conformity, universalism | sphere: prot.W | chance: 65
- U | ask him where the rest of the pipe has gone, and who buys it | v: self-direction | sphere: prot.U | chance: 65
- B | arrest him, and make sure the station knows it was your catch | act: arrest him, and make sure the station knows it was their catch | v: achievement, power | sphere: prot.B | chance: 65
- R | stand between him and the gate, and talk him down until help comes | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: prot.R | chance: 65
- G | ask his name and his street, and work out whose family he is | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: prot.G | chance: 65
- BG | take him in, and tell the custody desk about the children | v: benevolence, security | sphere: prot.BG | chance: 55
- RG | walk him to the van yourself, talking all the way, so he stays calm | act: walk him to the van themselves, talking all the way, so he stays calm | v: benevolence | sphere: prot.RG | chance: 55
- UB | offer to put in a good word if he names the buyer | v: power, security | sphere: prot.UB | chance: 55
- WR | radio it in at once, and keep him safe and still until the van comes | v: security, conformity | sphere: prot.RW | chance: 55
- WU | write every word he says in the notebook before anything else | v: conformity, achievement | sphere: prot.WU | chance: 55
works: The arrest stands up in court, and {mentor} says {N} did it as well as anyone could have.
works: Months later the man passes {N} on the street with a job and a nod.
fails: The paperwork is wrong in one place, and the case goes nowhere.
fails: {N} goes home and cannot stop thinking about the three children.

# ================================================================ the host (prot.host) and the families at home

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: the first day in uniform (pairs D1a)

== the first day in uniform
tier: life event
sphere: prot
stages: young_adult adult
age: 18-45
per_year: 0 0 .006 .002 0 0
drivers: unrest+.5 harsh+.2 prosper-.2
once: yes
times: Joining the police, the fire service, the forces, the prison service or a guard firm with an oath or a passing-out comes to about 1 in 10 lives (estimate; far more where service is compulsory, which 'the call to serve' covers), set at 6 in 1,000 a year in the twenties and fewer after
likelier: a family in uniform, a town with a barracks or a big station, few other jobs, unrest
rarer: a family that distrusts the force, good work elsewhere, poor health
gap: 1-2
tone: joy
life: work, duty, family
horizon: years
roles: parent, mentor
who: parent
earth: the passing-out parade: the oath said aloud, the new uniform, and your family in the stands
scene: Twelve weeks of training end on the parade ground. {N} stands in the new uniform with the rest of the intake and says the oath aloud; {parent} is in the stands, and tomorrow is the first real shift.
scene W: The oath is the same words for every one of them, rich or poor, and binds them to keep the peace the same for everyone. {N} means every word.
scene U: {N} looks along the line and wonders which of them will still be here in ten years, and what will decide it.
scene B: The postings list goes up tonight. The right first posting can set a whole career going.
scene R: {Ns} chest is tight with pride. The band strikes up, and {N} could march for miles.
scene G: {Ns} grandparent wore this uniform once. {parent} has the old photograph in a pocket, and keeps touching it.
- W | say every word of the oath as if it binds you for life | act: say every word of the oath as if it binds them for life | v: conformity, tradition | lever: loyalty | sphere: prot.W | chance: 65
- U | ask the instructors which postings teach most, and put in for one | v: self-direction, achievement | sphere: prot.U | chance: 65
- B | ask for the posting with the most overtime and the quickest promotion | v: achievement, power | sphere: prot.B | chance: 65
- R | ask for the busiest station in the city, starting tomorrow | v: stimulation | sphere: prot.R | chance: 65
- G | ask to be posted back home, to the streets you grew up on | act: ask to be posted back home, to the streets they grew up on | v: tradition, security | mark: came home | sphere: prot.G | chance: 65
- WU | keep your training notes, and go over the rules again each night | act: keep their training notes, and go over the rules again each night | v: conformity, achievement | sphere: prot.WU | chance: 55
- WR | volunteer for the night response team from the first week | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: prot.RW | chance: 55
- UG | ask an old officer from home what the job was like in their day | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: prot.GU | chance: 55
- BR | take the whole intake out to celebrate, and pick up the bill | v: hedonism, power | mark: made a friend | sphere: prot.BR | chance: 55
- BG | ask the veteran instructor for the plain truth about the work | v: security, tradition | sphere: prot.BG | chance: 55
works: The first months go well, and {N} finds the work fits better than they had hoped.
works: {parent} keeps the parade photograph on the dresser, and {N} catches them showing it to the neighbours.
fails: The first posting is nothing like the training, and {N} spends a hard year finding their feet.
fails: A bad first week with a hard sergeant sours the start, and {N} wonders whether to stay.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: the farewell at the gate (pairs D5a)

== the farewell at the barracks fence
tier: life event
sphere: prot
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-90
per_year: 0 .004 .005 .004 .003 .001
drivers: unrest+1 harsh+.2
times: Seeing a brother or sister off on a long posting with the forces comes to about 1 in 5 lives (estimate; many more in wartime or where service is compulsory), set at 4 to 5 in 1,000 a year
likelier: a brother or sister in the forces, a family in uniform, a war or a threat at the border
rarer: an only child, peace and a small professional army, a family that keeps out of the forces
gap: 2-10
tone: mixed
life: family, worry
horizon: months
roles: sibling, parent
who: sibling
earth: your brother or sister leaves from the barracks gate for a long posting, and the family stands at the fence
scene: {sibling} leaves for a nine-month posting far away. The family stands at the barracks fence at dawn as the buses fill; {parent} has not slept, and {sibling} keeps making jokes that nobody laughs at.
scene W: The families stand in a line along the fence, and there is a way to do this: no tears in front of them, a wave, and back to work.
scene U: {N} has read about where the posting is, and knows more than {parent} does. {N} decides how much of it to say.
scene B: {N} knows what helps out there: money, a phone that works, and nobody at home falling apart.
scene R: {N} wants to climb the fence, grab {sibling}, and make them laugh one more time before the bus.
scene G: {sibling} has never been further than the coast. The whole street has come out, and so have the cousins.
- W | stand straight and wave until the bus is gone, as the families do | v: tradition, conformity | sphere: prot.W | chance: 65
- U | ask how and when you can reach them out there, and write it all down | act: ask how and when they can reach them out there, and write it all down | v: security, self-direction | sphere: prot.U | chance: 65
- B | slip them some money for the posting, and say only what helps | v: benevolence, security | sphere: prot.B | chance: 65
- R | push through to the front, and hug them one last time | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: prot.R | chance: 65
- G | give them the family's old keepsake to carry, and ask for it back | v: tradition | sphere: prot.G | chance: 65
- BG | tell them plainly to keep their head down and just come home | v: security, benevolence | sphere: prot.BG | chance: 55
- UB | set up one family chat, so news from the posting reaches everyone at once | v: security | tech: phone | sphere: prot.UB | chance: 55
- UR | record a message from everyone at home, for them to play on the first bad night | v: benevolence, self-direction | sphere: prot.UR | chance: 55
- WG | promise to look after the family at home until they are back | v: benevolence, tradition | lever: loyalty | sphere: prot.GW | chance: 55
- WR | make them promise to write every week, and promise the same | v: benevolence, conformity | sphere: prot.RW | chance: 55
works: The posting passes, {sibling} comes home safe in the spring, and the family meets the bus at the same fence.
works: The letters and calls keep the family close through the months apart.
fails: The goodbye goes wrong: a sharp word at the fence that {N} replays for months.
fails: The months drag, the news is thin, and the worry settles into the house like damp.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: a comrade lost (pairs D4a)

== a comrade lost on the mountain road
tier: life event
sphere: prot
haunt: prot.host
ladder: regular
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 19-60
per_year: 0 0 .02 .015 .01 0
drivers: unrest+1.5 harsh+.3
times: Among those serving in the forces (haunt prot.host), losing someone from one's own unit comes to about 1 in 6 over a career in peacetime, mostly through accidents and illness (estimate), and far more in war, which the drivers raise
likelier: a war, hard postings, long road moves, a big unit
rarer: peace, a desk posting, a short term of service
gap: 3-10
tone: trouble
life: grief, work, friends
horizon: years
roles: colleague
who: colleague
earth: a soldier from your section dies when a truck goes off a mountain road at night, and the unit gathers to say goodbye
scene: Word comes at breakfast: {colleague}, who shared {Ns} room for two years, died when a truck went off the mountain road in the night. The unit is stood down for the day, and nobody knows what to do with their hands.
scene W: There is a way the unit honours its own, and {N} holds on to it: the parade, the folded flag, the names.
scene U: {N} keeps asking the same question: the road, the hour, the driver's shift. Why that truck, and why that night?
scene B: The posting still has months to run. {N} knows the only way through is to keep their head and their routine.
scene R: {N} wants to shout at someone, anyone. {colleague} was the loudest laugh in the section.
scene G: {colleague}'s family live three hours away, in a village {N} has heard about every night for two years.
